{%- comment -%} Styles live in assets/ha-sections.css, loaded once in layout/theme.liquid. {%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Hartwick Atelier — THE MASTERS. One section, two compositions.

    layout: index    Wireframe (01) HOMEPAGE §04 — dark field, editorial intro
                     left, the index of Masters centre, collection link right.

    layout: feature  Wireframe (03) PRODUCT PAGE §09 / mobile brief §7 — the same
                     dark field, but with a display heading, a numbered list of
                     the roles behind THIS garment, and portrait + workshop
                     images. "The Masters section remains a strong tonal shift,
                     using the dark field to distinguish human knowledge from
                     standard product information."

  Shared, as the audit planned (audit-and-plan.md §C: Meet the Masters is one
  component used on both pages). The data path, the placeholder path, the
  terminology and the touch states are written once; only the grid differs, and
  that difference lives in CSS.

  Terminology: The Masters. Never "The Makers" — the mobile brief is superseded
  on terminology by Framework v3 (CLAUDE.md).

  Data: the `master` metaobject (docs/data-model.md §2). Source is either the
  whole shop or, on a product page, this product's own hartwick.masters list.
  The moment those entries exist in Shopify they render here with no further
  work. Until then the wireframe's roles render as placeholders. Roles and
  regions only — no artisan name is ever invented, and names publish only when
  Aloha supplies them.

  ⚠️ COUNT CONFLICT — flagged to Aloha. The wireframe lists five roles; the
  mobile brief §7 records that "Angela would like us to feature three Masters
  initially". Built with five placeholder roles and a "Masters shown" limit, so
  either answer is a setting, not a rebuild.

  Accessibility (brief §7): there is no hover state on mobile, so every role is a
  visible link with a focus state and a 44px touch target. Portraits and workshop
  images take meaningful alt text; nothing here depends on hovering.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign is_feature = false
  if section.settings.layout == 'feature'
    assign is_feature = true
  endif

  # On a product page the Masters shown are the ones who made THIS garment.
  assign masters = nil
  if section.settings.source == 'product'
    assign masters = product.metafields.hartwick.masters.value
  else
    assign masters = shop.metaobjects.master.values
  endif

  assign limit = section.settings.item_limit
  assign use_placeholders = true
  if masters != blank and masters.size > 0
    assign use_placeholders = false
  endif

  # --- background photograph (Aloha, 4 September 2026) ---------------------
  # The mobile crop falls back to the desktop file, so one upload is enough to
  # see the section working and a second is an improvement, not a requirement.
  assign bg_d = section.settings.bg_image
  assign bg_m = section.settings.bg_image_mobile | default: bg_d
  assign has_bg = false
  if bg_d != blank
    assign has_bg = true
  endif

  # Focal point. Shopify's own image picker lets an editor drag the focus on the
  # file itself, and that is the control Aloha asked for — it travels with the
  # image rather than living in a section setting that has to be reset every
  # time the photograph is replaced. `presentation.focal_point` renders as
  # "50.0% 50.0%", exactly the shape object-position wants. The two selects
  # below only override it when an editor deliberately picks something else.
  assign focal_d = bg_d.presentation.focal_point | default: 'center center'
  if section.settings.bg_position != 'focal'
    assign focal_d = section.settings.bg_position
  endif
  assign focal_m = bg_m.presentation.focal_point | default: 'center center'
  if section.settings.bg_position_mobile != 'focal'
    assign focal_m = section.settings.bg_position_mobile
  endif
-%}

<section
  class="ha-section ha-masters ha-masters--{{ section.settings.layout }}{% if has_bg %} ha-masters--photo{% endif %}{% if section.settings.field == 'peat' or section.settings.field == blank %} ha-section--field-peat{% elsif section.settings.field != 'page' %} ha-section--field-{{ section.settings.field }}{% endif %}"
  {% if has_bg %}style="
    --ha-masters-scrim: {{ section.settings.bg_overlay | divided_by: 100.0 }};
    --ha-masters-focal: {{ focal_d }};
    --ha-masters-focal-m: {{ focal_m }};
    --ha-masters-ratio: {{ section.settings.bg_ratio }};
    --ha-masters-ratio-m: {{ section.settings.bg_ratio_mobile }};
  "{% endif %}
>
  {%- if has_bg -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      THE BACKGROUND PHOTOGRAPH — Aloha, 4 September 2026:
      "In the Handcrafted Modern reference, the full-width photograph is an
      important part of the section's structure. The text sits over the image
      rather than appearing on a plain colour block."

      Three things this markup is careful about:

      1. NO LAYOUT MOVEMENT. The image is absolutely positioned and fills the
         section, so it is out of normal flow and contributes exactly zero to
         the section's height — it cannot shift anything as it decodes. The
         reserved proportion Aloha asked for is held separately, by a
         min-height on the section computed from --ha-masters-ratio, so the
         composition holds its shape from first paint whether the file has
         arrived or not. Belt and braces: the shape is reserved AND the image
         cannot move it.

      2. EVERY WORD STAYS LIVE. Nothing here is text-in-an-image. The
         photograph is a <picture> behind the grid; the roles, the intro and
         the link are the same real, selectable, translatable, screen-reader
         -readable elements they were on the flat field.

      3. THE FLAT FIELD IS STILL THERE. It sits underneath as the loading and
         failure state, so a slow connection sees the section it saw before
         rather than unreadable text on white.

      Decorative by default: the section's meaning is carried by the live text,
      so an empty alt keeps a screen reader from announcing atmosphere as
      content. Filling in "Background alt text" opts back in when the chosen
      photograph is doing real editorial work.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="ha-masters__bg" {% if section.settings.bg_alt == blank %}aria-hidden="true"{% endif %}>
      <picture>
        {%- if bg_m != blank -%}
          <source
            media="(max-width: 749px)"
            srcset="{{ bg_m | image_url: width: 750 }} 750w, {{ bg_m | image_url: width: 1100 }} 1100w, {{ bg_m | image_url: width: 1500 }} 1500w"
            sizes="100vw"
          >
        {%- endif -%}
        <img
          src="{{ bg_d | image_url: width: 1600 }}"
          srcset="{{ bg_d | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w, {{ bg_d | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w, {{ bg_d | image_url: width: 1600 }} 1600w, {{ bg_d | image_url: width: 2000 }} 2000w, {{ bg_d | image_url: width: 2600 }} 2600w"
          sizes="100vw"
          width="{{ bg_d.width }}"
          height="{{ bg_d.height }}"
          alt="{{ section.settings.bg_alt | escape }}"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          class="ha-masters__bg-img"
        >
      </picture>
      <span class="ha-masters__scrim"></span>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="ha-wrap">
    <div class="ha-masters__grid">
      <div class="ha-masters__lead">
        {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
          <p class="ha-eyebrow ha-record">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if is_feature and section.settings.heading != blank -%}
          <h2 class="ha-display ha-narrate ha-masters__heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.intro != blank -%}
          <div class="ha-masters__intro ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.intro }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- render 'ha-placeholder-note', show: section.settings.show_placeholder_note -%}
      </div>

      <div class="ha-masters__body">
        {%- if section.settings.list_label != blank and is_feature == false -%}
          <p class="ha-eyebrow ha-record ha-masters__label">{{ section.settings.list_label }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        <ul class="ha-masters__list">
          {%- if use_placeholders -%}
            {%- for block in section.blocks limit: limit -%}
              <li class="ha-masters__item ha-narrate" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                {%- if is_feature -%}
                  <span class="ha-masters__num ha-record" aria-hidden="true">{{ forloop.index | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
                <span class="ha-masters__role">
                  {{- block.settings.role -}}
                  {%- if block.settings.region != blank -%}
                    &nbsp;·&nbsp;<span class="ha-masters__region">{{ block.settings.region }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </span>
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- for master in masters limit: limit -%}
              <li class="ha-masters__item ha-narrate">
                {%- if is_feature -%}
                  <span class="ha-masters__num ha-record" aria-hidden="true">{{ forloop.index | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if master.handle != blank and section.settings.link_masters -%}
                  <a class="ha-masters__role" href="{{ section.settings.masters_page_url }}#{{ master.handle }}">
                {%- else -%}
                  <span class="ha-masters__role">
                {%- endif -%}
                {{- master.role -}}
                {%- if master.region.value.place != blank -%}
                  &nbsp;·&nbsp;<span class="ha-masters__region">{{ master.region.value.place }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if master.handle != blank and section.settings.link_masters -%}
                  </a>
                {%- else -%}
                  </span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
            {%- if masters.size > limit -%}
              <li class="ha-masters__more ha-narrate" aria-hidden="true">[…]</li>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </ul>
      </div>

      {%- if is_feature -%}
        <div class="ha-masters__media">
          {%- liquid
            assign portrait = section.settings.portrait_image
            assign workshop = section.settings.workshop_image
            unless use_placeholders
              assign first = masters.first
              assign portrait = portrait | default: first.portrait.value
              assign workshop = workshop | default: first.workshop_images.value.first
            endunless
          -%}
          {%- render 'ha-figure',
            image: portrait,
            label: section.settings.portrait_label,
            class: 'ha-masters__figure',
            sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 20vw, 50vw',
            alt: section.settings.portrait_alt
          -%}
          {%- render 'ha-figure',
            image: workshop,
            label: section.settings.workshop_label,
            class: 'ha-masters__figure',
            sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 20vw, 50vw',
            alt: section.settings.workshop_alt
          -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Last in the DOM so the mobile stack reads intro → roles → images → link,
        exactly as the mobile wireframe does. Desktop lifts it back into the
        first column with explicit grid placement.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="ha-masters__cta">
        {%- if section.settings.cta_text != blank -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign cta = section.settings.cta_text

            # The count is opt-in now. "Meet the Masters [14] pieces" reads as a
            # collection link wearing the wrong label — a piece count answers a
            # question about the shop, not about the people.
            if section.settings.cta_show_count and is_feature == false
              if section.settings.cta_collection != blank
                assign cta = cta | append: ' [' | append: section.settings.cta_collection.products_count | append: '] pieces'
              elsif section.settings.cta_suffix != blank
                assign cta = cta | append: ' ' | append: section.settings.cta_suffix
              endif
            endif

            # An explicit link wins over the collection: the collection is only
            # bound to read a count from, and binding one must not silently
            # redirect a link that says "Meet the Masters". Falls back to the
            # same Masters page the roles above already link into.
            assign cta_href = section.settings.cta_link
            assign cta_href = cta_href | default: section.settings.cta_collection.url
            assign cta_href = cta_href | default: section.settings.masters_page_url
            assign cta_href = cta_href | default: '#'
          -%}
          <a class="ha-link ha-record" href="{{ cta_href }}">{{ cta }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "HA — Masters",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "ha-section-wrapper",
  "max_blocks": 12,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "select", "id": "field", "label": "Field colour", "default": "peat", "options": [
      { "value": "page", "label": "Page ground" },
      { "value": "white", "label": "White" },
      { "value": "peat", "label": "Peat (dark)" },
      { "value": "clay", "label": "Clay" },
      { "value": "botanical", "label": "Botanical" },
      { "value": "slate", "label": "Slate (dark)" }
    ] },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "layout",
      "label": "Layout",
      "options": [
        { "value": "index", "label": "Index (homepage)" },
        { "value": "feature", "label": "Feature (product page)" }
      ],
      "default": "index"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "source",
      "label": "Masters shown",
      "options": [
        { "value": "shop", "label": "All Masters" },
        { "value": "product", "label": "This product's Masters" }
      ],
      "default": "shop",
      "info": "'This product's Masters' reads hartwick.masters and only works on a product page."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "The Masters Index" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Knowledge held in human hands.", "info": "Feature layout only." },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "intro", "label": "Intro", "default": "<p>The practices, works and stories behind each collection. The people who hold the knowledge are never background.</p>" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "list_label", "label": "List label", "default": "Featured Masters", "info": "Index layout only." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "item_limit", "min": 3, "max": 16, "step": 1, "label": "Masters shown", "default": 9 },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "link_masters", "label": "Link each Master to The Masters page", "default": true },
    { "type": "url", "id": "masters_page_url", "label": "The Masters page" },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Background photograph",
      "info": "A full-width workshop, process or Master photograph behind the whole section. The three-column structure and every word of text stay live on top of it. Leave empty for the flat field."
    },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "bg_image", "label": "Background — desktop", "info": "Drag the focal point on the image itself in the picker; the section follows it." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "bg_image_mobile", "label": "Background — mobile crop", "info": "Optional. Falls back to the desktop photograph." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "bg_alt", "label": "Background alt text", "info": "Leave empty to treat the photograph as decorative — correct while every word of the section is live text." },
    {
      "type": "range", "id": "bg_overlay", "min": 0, "max": 90, "step": 5, "unit": "%",
      "label": "Dark overlay", "default": 60,
      "info": "Restrains the photograph so the text stays readable. Below about 45% check the palest part of the picture before approving."
    },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "bg_position", "label": "Focus — desktop", "default": "focal",
      "info": "'Follow the image' uses the focal point set on the file itself.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "focal", "label": "Follow the image" },
        { "value": "center center", "label": "Centre" },
        { "value": "center top", "label": "Top" },
        { "value": "center bottom", "label": "Bottom" },
        { "value": "left center", "label": "Left" },
        { "value": "right center", "label": "Right" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "bg_position_mobile", "label": "Focus — mobile", "default": "focal",
      "options": [
        { "value": "focal", "label": "Follow the image" },
        { "value": "center center", "label": "Centre" },
        { "value": "center top", "label": "Top" },
        { "value": "center bottom", "label": "Bottom" },
        { "value": "left center", "label": "Left" },
        { "value": "right center", "label": "Right" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "bg_ratio", "label": "Reserved proportion — desktop", "default": "1.7778",
      "info": "The shape the section holds from first paint, so nothing moves while the photograph loads.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "2.3333", "label": "21:9 — cinematic" },
        { "value": "1.7778", "label": "16:9 — wide" },
        { "value": "1.5",    "label": "3:2" },
        { "value": "1.3333", "label": "4:3" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "bg_ratio_mobile", "label": "Reserved proportion — mobile", "default": "0.8",
      "options": [
        { "value": "1.3333", "label": "4:3" },
        { "value": "1",      "label": "1:1" },
        { "value": "0.8",    "label": "4:5 — upright" },
        { "value": "0.75",   "label": "3:4 — upright" }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Images", "info": "Feature layout only. Falls back to the first Master's portrait and workshop image." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "portrait_image", "label": "Portrait" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "portrait_alt", "label": "Portrait alt text" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "portrait_label", "label": "Portrait placeholder label", "default": "01 / Portrait" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "workshop_image", "label": "Workshop" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "workshop_alt", "label": "Workshop alt text" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "workshop_label", "label": "Workshop placeholder label", "default": "02 / Workshop" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Link" },
    {
      "type": "text", "id": "cta_text", "label": "Link text", "default": "Meet the Masters",
      "info": "Aloha, 4 September 2026: point this at the Masters, not the collection, unless the collection genuinely shows only pieces made by the Masters listed here."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox", "id": "cta_show_count", "label": "Append the piece count", "default": false,
      "info": "A count belongs on a collection link. Leave off for 'Meet the Masters'."
    },
    { "type": "collection", "id": "cta_collection", "label": "Collection", "info": "Only used when the link points at a collection. The piece count is read from here." },
    { "type": "url", "id": "cta_link", "label": "Link (if no collection)" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_suffix", "label": "Placeholder count", "default": "[14] pieces", "info": "Used only while no collection is set, and only when the count is switched on." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Provisional content" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_placeholder_note", "label": "Show placeholder notice", "default": true }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "master",
      "name": "Placeholder Master",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "role", "label": "Role" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "region", "label": "Region" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Hartwick — The Masters Index" }]
}
{% endschema %}
